# Project Workflow & Safety

## Secrets hygiene (must follow)

- Never commit real passwords, tokens, private keys, or connection strings.
- `.env` and `backend/keys/` are local-only and must stay gitignored.
- `.env.example` may exist in git, but it must contain **placeholders only** (e.g., `change-me-before-starting`).
- If a tracked file accidentally contains credentials, remove them immediately and move configuration to env vars.

## Plan tracking (must follow)

- Keep `doc/plan/PLAN_v1.0.md` up to date:
  - When a checklist item is finished, flip `[ ]` → `[x]` in the same change-set.
  - Do not mark items complete unless at least one real verification was run.

## Database migrations (must follow)

- Treat migrations as immutable. Do not edit an old migration after it has been applied.
- Fix forward: create a new migration with the next sequence number.

## Verification before “done” (must follow)

- Before claiming a phase/task is complete, run at least one relevant check:
  - Backend: `go build ./...` and/or a smoke endpoint call
  - Frontend: `npm run build`
  - DB: confirm migrations applied (tables/views exist) and a minimal flow works

